{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789292750,"nonce":"BMslqdqBfJw/he59YGixs5ABbtE=","title":"Python: the standard library modules beyond math, sys and typing","message":"`stdlib.rs` resolves math, sys and typing; anything else is refused\nwith \"import of module `x`\". In rough order of how often scripts want\nthem:\n\n1. random: seed, random, randint, randrange, choice, shuffle, uniform.\n   Matching CPython's output needs MT19937 with its init_by_array\n   seeding, genrand_res53 for random() and _randbelow's getrandbits\n   rejection loop; without that, tests can only check ranges.\n2. time: time, perf_counter, sleep, monotonic; non-deterministic, so\n   conformance can only check monotonicity.\n3. collections: defaultdict, Counter, deque, namedtuple, OrderedDict.\n   defaultdict and Counter are dict subclasses (d3acf39 territory);\n   deque is a list with O(1) ends.\n4. itertools: chain, product, permutations, combinations, count,\n   islice, groupby, accumulate; functools: reduce, lru_cache, partial.\n   Most are eager lists here (lazy iterators are 4f32f29).\n5. os / os.path: getcwd, listdir, path.join/exists/basename, environ;\n   need a filesystem plugin (zrtl_fs exists).\n6. string: ascii_letters, digits, punctuation; constants only.\n7. re: a regex engine, or a plugin; largest single item.\n8. json: loads/dumps over dict/list/str/int/float/bool/None; zrtl_json\n   exists.\n9. dataclasses, enum, abc: class machinery (d3acf39).","files":null}]}